        ":question/id": "3b89344e-126d-544e-88e0-0303a3eae594",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-103354",
        ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y=0\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y & =0 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,y & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\right)y & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)y & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}_{P(x)}y & =\\underbrace{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$"
      },
